.TH ENCODER 1 "2026-11-06" "KEncoder" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
encoder \- control HP OMEN Encoder keyboard backlighting from the command line
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B encoder
.RB [ \-b " " 0|1|2|3 ]
.RB [ \-s | \-o | \-a " " MODE ]
.RB [ \-v " " SPEED ]
.br
.B encoder --status [--json]
.br
.B encoder -h
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B encoder
sets the brightness and backlighting mode of the HP OMEN Encoder
keyboard (USB VID:PID 03f0:3341) using the Linux HID raw interface.
It provides static backlighting, lighting off, and several animation
effects.
.PP
The program locates the matching device
.I /dev/hidrawX
using its USB identifiers and the HID report descriptor size.
The interface must be accessible for both reading and writing.
Ordinary commands change the device settings. The
.B --status
option instead reads the currently reported brightness and effect
family without changing the backlighting.
Wave direction and animation speed cannot currently be read back.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --status
Performs a read-only GetDeviceInfo (80 01) query without sending any
brightness or effect-setting commands.
Reports whether lighting is on or off, brightness from 0 to 3, and
the effect family. Wave direction and animation speed remain
unknown.
Cannot be combined with options that write device settings.
.TP
.B --json
When used with --status, prints machine-readable JSON.
The direction and speed fields are always null; the source field is
hardware.
.TP
.B \-h
Prints brief help and exits. A connected keyboard is not required.
.TP
.B \-s
Turns on static key backlighting.
.TP
.B \-o
Turns off the backlighting.
.TP
.BI \-b " LEVEL"
Sets brightness to 0, 1, 2, or 3; higher values produce brighter
light.
When omitted, the current implementation uses level 3.
Brightness may also be set alone without changing the current
lighting mode.
.TP
.BI \-a " MODE"
Selects an animation. Supported values are:
.RS
.TP
.B ripple
Ripple effect.
.TP
.B left_wave
Wave from the left.
.TP
.B right_wave
Wave from the right.
.TP
.B breathe
Pulsing or breathing effect.
.RE
.TP
.BI \-v " SPEED"
Animation speed: slow, medium, or fast.
The default is slow.
Only takes effect with -a; setting speed without an animation has no
visible effect.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B encoder -b 1 -s
Set brightness to 1 and turn on static lighting.
.TP
.B encoder -b 3 -a ripple -v fast
Set brightness to 3 and enable fast ripples.
.TP
.B encoder -a left_wave -v medium
Start a medium-speed wave from the left; brightness defaults to 3
without -b.
.TP
.B encoder -b 2
Set only brightness to 2, without changing the lighting mode.
.TP
.B encoder -o
Turn off backlighting.
.TP
.B encoder -h
Print the help message.
.SH OPTION ORDER AND COMBINATIONS
The program sends the brightness setting first, followed by the
command to turn lighting off, select static lighting, or start an
animation.
This also applies when -o is used or when the program is invoked
without options.
If multiple mode options are given, -o takes precedence, followed by
-s and then -a. Specify only one mode option for predictable
behavior.
.PP
The current implementation does not always report unknown arguments
or unsupported values as errors.
The --status option uses a separate read-only path and never sends a
lighting-setting command.
.SH PERMISSIONS AND DEVICE
.B encoder
opens the corresponding
.I /dev/hidrawX
interface for reading and writing.
Access can be granted by the udev rule shipped with the encoder
package or by administrator permissions.
If the keyboard is disconnected, the interface is not found, or
access is denied, the program prints:
.PP
.nf
OMEN Encoder keyboard not found or access denied
.fi
.PP
If this happens, check that the keyboard is connected and that the
HID raw device permissions allow access. The path
.I /dev/hidrawX
may change after reconnecting the keyboard.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Help was displayed, or the request was processed without an error
opening the device.
In the current implementation, exit status 0 does not necessarily
mean the device confirmed every HID command.
.TP
.B 1
The matching keyboard could not be opened (not found or permission
denied). For read-only status mode, it also indicates a
communication error or an unsupported response format.
.TP
.B 2
An invalid combination of options involving --status or --json.
.PP
Communication failures for older write commands may be displayed as
.B Command failed
without an accompanying nonzero exit status. Read-only status mode
writes error messages to standard error.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /dev/hidrawX
HID raw interface of the compatible keyboard.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/udev/rules.d/
Device access rules installed by the package.
